Description:

A WebDAV LOCK now honours the client's Timeout header ("Second-N" or
"Infinite", RFC 4918), up to the new dav_writelock_max_timeout.  Previously
every lock lasted five minutes whatever the client asked for.


Documentation:

lib/imapoptions/dav_writelock_max_timeout


Config changes:

New option dav_writelock_max_timeout (duration, default 5m).


Upgrade instructions:

None.  With the default, a lock still lasts at most five minutes; a client
that asks for less now gets what it asked for.  To allow longer locks, raise
dav_writelock_max_timeout.


